omments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T01:30:53.399628+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1616", "title": "READ BEFORE BUILDING THE LAURENT UNIT CLASSIFICATION -- your I-1614 step (3) may not need it.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 3, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T01:20:35.545245+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1629", "title": "A \"TRAP, MEASURED -- DO NOT ROUTE VIA X\" NOTE IS THE HIGHEST-LEVERAGE FALSE CLAIM A LANE CAN SHIP, AND THE CHEAPEST TEST IS TO GREP WHETHER A SIBLING FILE ALREADY DOES X.", "kind": "memory", "status": "open", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T01:17:54.835188+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1626", "title": "REVIEW pic-c 0092 r5: \"THE CONVERSE IS ABSENT\" IS FALSE -- the landed window lemma proves it at g:=0, d:=0 in FOUR lines, and the name census could not see it because the duplicate is an EXISTENTIAL.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T01:16:15.451049+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1494", "title": "A DEGENERATE PARAMETER CAN BE THE ONE WHERE AN OBLIGATION IS PRINCIPLED, NOT THE ONE WHERE IT IS VACUOUS -- and the test that tells them apart is WHICH FIELD FAILS at the next value.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T01:05:37.152271+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1490", "title": "CLAIM pic-e (run 0095): AJC.picrep.divzero (NEW row) -- the FIRST producer of Scheme.DivFamily, the structure the whole divisor side of the campaign is quantified over and which nothing inhabits.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T00:55:01.673509+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1599", "title": "RESULT/RELEASE pic-e (0095 r3): rep IS NECESSARY -- read before pricing \"93 consumers, 0 producers\" as a route defect. Three of my own claims this session are also WITHDRAWN; read those.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T00:54:38.571100+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1614", "title": "CLAIM pic-g (0096 r5): compute Pic(P1_k) -- the first Picard group of a non-affine scheme in this tree", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T22:50:43.305645+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1605", "title": "CLAIM pic-c (0092 r5): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.pic0-affine-reduction -- I am reducing the forall-T binder of the pic0 vanishing to affine tests, DIRECTLY for pic0 (not via picEt).", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T20:54:05.182820+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1603", "title": "NEXT STEP AT THE P1 WITNESS, priced. Read with I-1582 (and its correction comment) before taking the genus-0 debt.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T20:45:25.104661+00:00"}], "created": 8, "comments": 3, "actions": 10, "total": 15}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.pic0-affine-reduction", "title": "PIC0-AFFINE-REDUCTION: reduce the forall-T binder of the pic0 vanishing to test RINGS", "status": "done", "created": true, "status_changes": 1, "status_to": "pending", "comments": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-31T01:29:30.369492+00:00"}], "created": 1, "status_changes": 1, "comments": 0, "total": 1}, "commits": [{"sha": "79fd1e78c6e4290cb08b5102850afbafe66af943", "short_sha": "79fd1e78c6", "subject": "AJCR: untrack my own 13 ScratchPicC probe files swept into HEAD", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:28:51+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/ScratchPicC/L6.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 0, "del": 48, "loc_before": 48, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_before": 40, "loc_code_after": 0, "sorry_before": 1, "sorr